; expect: exit 0
; More values live at once than there are registers (17), so the allocator
; must spill. a0..a23 are all defined before any is used, then folded with
; h = h * 3 + a_i from a23 down to a0. @pressure_call keeps them live across
; calls that clobber every caller-saved register, so only the 10
; callee-saved registers can hold them. Checked against C in
; regalloc_pressure.c.
decl @clobber()

